{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass, etc.</b> Its sense concerns the king of Assyria." "And the meaning of <b>miqdash</b> [sanctuary] is from the root that a person goes to it to magnify himself in it and to fortify himself in it. And behold, it is joined: 'a sanctuary' [equals] 'a stone of stumbling,' which a person goes up onto to seek refuge in it." "<b>For the two houses of Israel.</b> The kingdom of Israel and Judah." "And behold, the meaning of <b>lefach</b> [for a snare] is for Ephraim; <b>ulemoqesh</b> [and for a trap], for Judah."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:53.305256061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}